Simple approach: write a temp .tsx test and run vitest with node environment using renderToString. Gravity components in SSR should work (uikit supports SSR).

Actually simpler: vite can build a small SSR entry. Even simpler — use `vite-node`? Not installed. Let me just do a vitest one-liner test file outside src (vitest include default covers *.test.ts* anywhere). I'll create a temp test in workspace root, run vitest run, then delete. tsconfig includes only src, but vitest uses esbuild and doesn't care.

Test:
```tsx
import {renderToString} from 'react-dom/server';
import {ThemeProvider} from '@gravity-ui/uikit';
import {App} from './src/App';
import {it, expect} from 'vitest';

it('renders landing', () => {
  const html = renderToString(<ThemeProvider theme="light"><App/></ThemeProvider>);
  expect(html).toContain('Учёт времени команды');
  expect(html).toContain('Начните учитывать время');
});
```

Need JSX in test — .tsx file works with vitest + esbuild. React import needed? With jsx react-jsx transform esbuild handles via tsconfig? Vitest reads tsconfig jsx setting via esbuild? Vite's esbuild uses tsconfig's jsx field — yes, esbuild respects "jsx": "react-jsx" from tsconfig.

Where to place? /tmp would be outside vite root... vitest root is workspace. Put it at workspace root as smoke.test.tsx, run `npx vitest run smoke.test.tsx`, then remove. Gravity styles imports? App.tsx doesn't import CSS. Good.

